From: Nebur692 <nebur_692@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:57:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Tests: keep the backport tests that Remi's 7.2.34-32 lacks

Remi's 7.2.34-32 now carries the fixes this package used to backport on its
own (CVE-2025-1218, CVE-2025-1735, GH-11274...), but not all of their tests.
These are the tests of the previous php72-php-7.2.34-31.1.el8.legacy that
are missing from Remi's tree: the GHSA-r6x9-5r99-36j7 mysqlnd tests (with
the fake server functions they need, plus Remi's new
my_mysqli_test_ok_message_length_past_packet), GHSA-hrwm-9436-5mv3 for
pgsql and pdo_pgsql, and GH-11274. They prove that Remi's fixes behave
like ours.
